": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01KaPXVrRQG3iTAnoRA1YFYs", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53157, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01KaPXVrRQG3iTAnoRA1YFYs", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 54513, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_011uU9S98tNbTwm9UHgyr7Du", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 54813, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_011uU9S98tNbTwm9UHgyr7Du", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54813, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_011uU9S98tNbTwm9UHgyr7Du", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 58580, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The bad deploy was v2.3.1, and the v2.3.1-rc before it was also unhealthy. The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, leaving the other two regions on v2.3.1. I retried once and it finished. us-east, us-west and eu-west are now all on v2.3.0, and the error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) is open and has paged on-call. The create request timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying and found it had gone through. There's only one incident, no duplicate. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry), the current state, and two follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the orchestrator error.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SQLGmGTyCSNXYvGJ3ABfFy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014TdddJZYFogLiuWLc8ajSS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01LzrtvC381h6GYzt9zwSsJR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Mp5bqRHDXWRvBjWZjbwZ2F", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Setting the same target version again is safe, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Pi4aFp6ke6D78sEdK7NUBx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Et9vA935u31heDvHi83T5h", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01SpUYyY4K8MvBgPMvCiFD5o", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KaPXVrRQG3iTAnoRA1YFYs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release marked healthy (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy). The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, leaving the regions on different versions. A retry finished the rollback in us-west and eu-west. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and investigate the orchestrator error during rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_011uU9S98tNbTwm9UHgyr7Du", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The bad deploy was v2.3.1, and the v2.3.1-rc before it was also unhealthy. The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, leaving the other two regions on v2.3.1. I retried once and it finished. us-east, us-west and eu-west are now all on v2.3.0, and the error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) is open and has paged on-call. The create request timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying and found it had gone through. There's only one incident, no duplicate. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry), the current state, and two follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the orchestrator error.", "type": "text"}]}]}